      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this term in Case 16-285, Epic Systems Corporation versus Lewis, and the consolidated cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is that a concession that this is a concerted action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But the courthouse, Mr. Clement -- Mr. Clement, the courthouse is not at issue here as I understand it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But putting that aside, I'm not sure that the FAA is now a rule of statutory construction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Is one understanding of Title VII says to the employer, you shall not discriminate, and Section 7 says to the employer, you shall not interfere with concerted activity, such as three guys joining together to bring a suit if they want to."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF RICHARD D. GRIFFIN, ESQ., ON BEHALF OF PETITIONER, ACTING AS RESPONDENT IN NO. 16-307"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Board's precedent has always said that individual agreements that require employees to individually waive their right to proceed collectively are violations of the National Labor Relations Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: And the other question I have is, how do you draw a distinction between a -- an agreement precluding class arbitration and all of the other Rules of Civil Procedure that limit the ability of employees to engage in collective litigation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Academy of Arbitrators",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Academy of Arbitrators filed a brief -- amicus brief in this case, Your Honor, supporting the position that the Board took in Murphy Oil, and it addresses the circumstances under which, in both labor arbitration and employment arbitration, employees are able to proceed in joint collective representative actions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF DANIEL R. ORTIZ, ESQ., ON BEHALF OF RESPONDENTS IN NOS. 16-285 AND 16-300"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ortiz",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ORTIZ: Your Honor, under Section 7, as long as joint legal action is available in one forum, that would be sufficient."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce3963c53a937f2b7dd7bfe95cfffe43047f2f566b506ecf0571af2a0379102a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce3963c53a93-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about the confidentiality agreements which, I take it, puts a damper on how -- how jointly these people can proceed?"
    },
    {
